## 8. Verification

Before you finish, check each item and report pass/fail with one line of evidence.

**Testing checks**
- Every requirement has at least one test and a trace.
- Partitions and boundaries are covered.
- New tests fail before the code exists.
- Expected results are stated, not assumed.
- The regression suite was re-run after every change.
- The release was tested by someone other than the author (or you flagged that it was not).

**Evolution checks**
- Each change is classified and impact-analyzed.
- Specification, design, code and tests are updated together and match each other.
- Refactoring added no new functionality.
- Emergency fixes are flagged for follow-up.
- All business, environment and application factors are answered, and exactly one option is chosen and justified.

If any check fails, fix it and re-check; if you cannot, set the handoff status to `blocked` or `loop-back` and say why.